    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **64 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key and duplicate detection as specified.\n\n**New identity key** (`IdentityKeys.java`): now the 64-char lowercase hex `SHA-256` of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`, replacing the old plain pipe-string that folded in `householdId`. Email is defensively re-lowercased; the last name goes through a new phonetic encoder.\n\n**New Soundex helper** (`Soundex.java`, common package): standard American Soundex (initial letter + three digits), shared by the key and the soft-match. Names that sound alike collapse to the same code.\n\n**Duplicate detection** (`RejectDuplicateIdentity.java`): reduced to the single identity key \u2014 a 409 fires only when a live owner's whole `identityKey` matches. The separate computed-`householdId` household-duplicate block (and its `sharesHousehold` bypass) is gone. Soft-deleted owners are still ignored, and the email-domain blocklist still runs first as an earlier pipeline step.\n\n**Soft match** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`): now triggers when `soundex(lastName)` and postcode match but the `identityKey` differs, rather than on lowercase-name + postcode + different-telephone. So two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones are created and the second is flagged `possibleDuplicate` \u2014 no longer a hard 409.\n\n**OpenAPI** (`openapi.yml`): updated the `identityKey` schema description and example to the new SHA-256 form.\n\nBehaviour notes preserved: `householdId` assignment (and the household-based membership-points/size logic) is unchanged, so the `sharesHousehold` household-membership tests still pass; declared household members remain exempt from soft-match flagging.",
